{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.matrixModel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.matrixModel","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.lean#L60-L88","doc":"**De-axiomatisation (concrete model, bean `cy3v`).** The `n×n` matrix\nalgebra over a field, with the matrix trace, is a genuine instance of the\nFrobenius carrier — the three axioms are *theorems*, not assumptions:\ncyclicity is `Matrix.trace_mul_comm` (a non-trivial fact in a\nnon-commutative algebra), additivity is `Matrix.trace_add`, and\nnon-degeneracy is witnessed by pairing a nonzero entry `A i j ≠ 0` against\nthe elementary matrix `E_{j,i}`, which gives `tr(A · E_{j,i}) = A i j`.\nSo the abstract carrier — hence the Frobenius self-duality — is realisable,\nnot vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.Obs_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.Obs_add","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.lean#L56-L58","doc":"The Observation Frame is additive in its argument (a linear functional). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.Obs_eq_pairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.Obs_eq_pairing","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.lean#L51-L54","doc":"`Obs` is exactly pairing against the observable, so the primal element\n`a` and its dual functional `Obs a` live in the same space (LP primal ↔\ndual identification). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.pairing_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.pairing_symm","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.lean#L46-L49","doc":"The Frobenius pairing is symmetric — the source of self-duality\n(`H_n ≅ H_n^*`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.Obs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.Obs","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.lean#L42-L44","doc":"The Observation Frame `Obs_τ(a) = τ(a · −)` (the shadow-price\nfunctional of the observable `a`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.pairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.pairing","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.lean#L39-L40","doc":"The Frobenius pairing `⟨a,b⟩ = τ(ab)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.nondegenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.nondegenerate","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.lean#L32-L32","doc":"Non-degeneracy: a nonzero element pairs non-trivially with something. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.tau_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.tau_add","kind":"theorem","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.lean#L30-L30","doc":"`τ` is additive (bilinearity of the induced pairing). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.tau_cyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.tau_cyclic","kind":"theorem","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.lean#L28-L28","doc":"Cyclic (Markov) symmetry `τ(ab) = τ(ba)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.τ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.τ","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.lean#L26-L26","doc":"The Markov trace `τ : A → R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.lean#L23-L23","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction","kind":"structure","line":18,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.lean#L18-L32","doc":"The Frobenius / Markov-trace data on an algebra `A`.\n\nA `definition` carrier: the trace `τ`, its cyclic-symmetry, and the\nnon-degeneracy witness (for every `a ≠ 0` some `b` pairs non-trivially) —\nexactly the data making `(A, τ)` Frobenius, hence self-dual. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:frobenius-self-duality-forces-lp-dual-extraction","label":"prop:frobenius-self-duality-forces-lp-dual-extraction","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-self-duality-forces-lp-dual-extraction.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}